.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt CMP 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmp
.Nd compare two files byte by byte (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l | Fl s
.Ar file1
.Ar file2
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm cmp ,
built unpatched for ABSD with the C kit; see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It reports the first byte and line where the two files differ;
.Fl l
lists every differing byte,
.Fl s
prints nothing and answers by status only.
A file named
.Ql -
is standard input.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
Nothing is refused.
Messages begin with the name the program was run as, and their
.Ql strerror
texts are Picolibc's.
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the files are the same, 1 when they differ, 2 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ cmp /home/operator/a.out /tmp/session-1/a.out
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr od 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
